      "design": "r2B",
      "good": "The slightly wider title column gives page names comfortable space, while the URL column keeps the same three-line maximum as r2A. Status codes remain easy to scan.",
      "problems": "The dates all split across two lines, interrupting comparison down the column. The extra title width produces little visible benefit over r2A, and both audit headers still wrap.",
      "cause": "The 96px date column leaves only 75px for text. Moving width from the date column to the title and URL columns does not change the observed row heights."
    },
    {
      "design": "r2C",
      "good": "Dates and both audit headers fit on one line, making the audit results clear and easy to compare. Status codes have ample separation from the dates.",
      "problems": "The narrow title column fragments several names, particularly the Salesforce title, and the first two URLs take four lines. The resulting tall rows leave substantial empty space in the audit columns.",
      "cause": "The 150px title column and 345px URL column leave less room for the identifying information. The 107px status column gives its short codes more space than they need."
    }
